  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "RDMA2-P1-001",
      "severity": "P1",
      "title": "The v2 schema accepts completed semantic and capitalization states forbidden by the neutral instructions",
      "affectedArtifacts": [
        "pilot/evaluation/v4/readjudication-instructions-v2.md",
        "pilot/evaluation/v4/readjudication-schema-v2.json",
        "docs/AI_MAPPING_V4_READJUDICATION_PREREGISTRATION_V2.md"
      ],
      "evidence": [
        "Neutral instructions define targetRelationToSource=exact as equal meaning scope and necessary conditions, while necessaryConditionsMatch=false means the necessary conditions do not match. The schema has no conditional that rejects exact together with a false semantic boolean.",
        "The fixed Korean-capitalization rule permits source-only-preservable when actual English capitalization evidence exists and unknown when it does not; it expressly forbids inferring Korean target conflict. The completed usage schema nevertheless permits capitalization=conflict, as well as every other generic usage enum value.",
        "The schema's completedAdjudication overlay only requires the semantic booleans and usage axes to be non-null. Its allOf consistency conditions cover example verdicts only, not these semantic or capitalization contradictions."
      ],
      "schemaAcceptedContradictionWitness": {
        "semantic": {
          "targetRelationToSource": "exact",
          "referentTypeMatch": false,
          "eventAndParticipantsMatch": true,
          "necessaryConditionsMatch": false
        },
        "usage": {
          "capitalization": "conflict"
        },
        "acceptanceBasis": "These values satisfy the completed enums and non-null types, and no schema conditional rejects either combination when embedded in an otherwise valid completed row."
      },
      "impact": "C and D can submit byte-identical, schema-valid but instruction-contradictory cores. The comparator would accept them as consensus, and gold derivation would count them as negatives rather than invalidating the round, potentially satisfying the minimum-negative gate with internally invalid cases.",
      "requiredDisposition": "Keep blank-form creation and execution prohibited. Preserve v2 unchanged and create a new sealed version whose schema mechanically rejects exact with any false semantic match boolean and restricts capitalization to the values permitted by the fixed Korean rule. Re-audit the new exact SHA set before creating forms."
    }
  ],
